(Per `unit-economics-saas` fragment: LTV / CAC ≥ 3 is the working threshold; ratios below 3 indicate either CAC bloat or LTV erosion. Pre-revenue projects use comparable-company benchmarks; established projects use cohort actuals.)

## Per-tenant attribution

| Cost category | Attribution mechanism | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| compute | {{attribution_compute}} | Every request span / log line carries `tenant_id`; rolls up to per-tenant compute cost. |
| storage | {{attribution_storage}} | Tenancy-coupled (see spec §3.R1): RLS → `by_predicate`; schema → `by_schema`; cell → `by_cell_then_intra`; hybrid → `mixed`. |
| network | {{attribution_network}} | Egress / data-transfer attributed via `X-Tenant-Id` header at the gateway. |
| third_party | {{attribution_third_party}} | Wrapped client SDKs (OpenAI, Stripe, S3 cross-region) log per-call cost + `tenant_id`. CRITICAL for AI workloads. |

**Coverage target (per `per-tenant-cost-attribution-with-hooks` fragment CRITICAL):** per-tenant cost rollup must reconcile to cloud-bill total within 95%. Unattributed waste indicates an instrumentation gap that becomes a pricing-margin leak at scale.

